      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jphacks/tkb_2615/git/trees/449541dabb6c953896bb8022234bfb4eda8f4928"
    },
    "message": "Make Runs of another model version view-only, without raising the version\n\nCheckpoints now record the whole-model version (engine:model, 1) and the\nRNG algorithm (engine:rng_algorithm) in model_signatures; a save without\nthem was computed by engine 1 (core/model_version.py). A save whose\nrecorded versions differ from the installed ones is restored for viewing\nonly (Checkpoint.restore_view, ProjectStore.load_view_checkpoint): its\nworld carries a mark that TickEngine, the controller, BranchRuntime and\nCheckpoint.capture refuse. Tick paths refuse it with run_model_view_only\nand a Japanese message instead of \"explicit migration required\".\n\nFor such a Run the timeline shows saved points only (D2): frame,\nview_at and iter_worlds round a minute between saves down to the saved\npoint, say so (saved_point_rounding, model_view) and never tick. The\nproject API, replay, history, comparison, PDF report, CLI and the demo\nread it; resume, fork, EffectPrograms, intervention previews and demo\njobs are refused before any worker starts. LEGACY_SHAPES_TICKABLE lets\nthe change that removes the Python migrations take the pre-queue FIFO\nmode and information schema 1 off the tick path.\n\nThe installed version stays 1, so results and hashes do not change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K4QyYRukuCLBerKa4UYj4y",
